invariant: INV-35
file: build.c
catches: test/lib-check-webpki-tcp-nonblocking.sh
reason: build.c writes the axes out as a union of its own and leaves out
  CH_BUILD_IF_TRANSPORT_TCP_NONBLOCKING, so a tcp-nonblocking object reports that it
  was built without CH_TRANSPORT_TCP_NONBLOCKING. Every size in its record is
  still right, and a consumer built with the define reads different
  axes. lib-check links test/build_test.c under the object's own
  defines, and that consumer must read a record equal to its headers,
  so it objects.

--- old
    .axes = CH_BUILD_AXES,
--- new
    .axes = CH_BUILD_IF_TRUST_CA | CH_BUILD_IF_TRUST_WEBPKI | CH_BUILD_IF_PIN_ECDSA |
            CH_BUILD_IF_KEX_PQ | CH_BUILD_IF_TRANSPORT_QUIC_NONBLOCKING | CH_BUILD_IF_SUITE_AES_GCM |
            CH_BUILD_IF_ROLE_SERVER | CH_BUILD_IF_EXPORTER | CH_BUILD_IF_KEYLOG,
